WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.394
 

00:00:02.692 --> 00:00:04.100
I mean sure

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.040
we need a little bit of everything in the world.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.060
I am an optimist.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.120
So we can tell the pessimists
the same thing,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.255
"Don't you want some optimism
in the world?"

00:00:12.255 --> 00:00:15.200
I believe in balance in the world and

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.200
where I get uncomfortable
and I think where life gets uncomfortable

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.380
is when we face imbalance.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.885
When there's too much pessimism
in the world

00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:25.740
I think it brings us all down.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.020
And the way to defeat pessimism
is with optimism.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.179
But at the same time
if all you have is optimists

00:00:30.179 --> 00:00:33.480
then I think we're all gonna be 
living in a cloud and

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.860
then we become blind as well.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.620
So I think balance is key.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.680
I do my job - 
I'm one of the optimists in the world.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.340
I frustrate pessimists

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.368
and we need pessimists in the world

00:00:45.368 --> 00:00:48.500
and I frustrate them.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.873
But yeah,
we need we need balance.

00:00:50.873 --> 00:00:52.849
Long-term needs short-term,

00:00:52.849 --> 00:00:54.824
short-term needs long-term,

00:00:54.824 --> 00:00:55.900
it's all the same thing.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.900
So I would rather have a slight
imbalance towards optimism.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.100
I would rather have a slight imbalance towards
long-term over short-term.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.100
I would rather have a slight imbalance of
people over profit.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.360
I don't think there's such thing as
perfect balance

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.360
there's no such thing as 50/50.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.500
At some point we're gonna face decisions
where something has to give.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.340
You can't have two things be equal all the time.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.260
And so I do believe in biases.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.132
So even though
yes we need pessimists

00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:23.740
we need slightly more optimists.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.760
Even though
yes we need short-term thinkers

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.540
we need slightly more long-term thinkers.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.923
Even though yes we need finite thinking

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.490
we need slightly more infinite thinking.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.000
and that kind of thing.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.400
 

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.900
I think

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.700
I'll take an imbalance towards the positive
any day.

